---
import ComputerLayout from "../layouts/ComputerLayout.astro";
---

<ComputerLayout
  title="Voice Dataset Builder | Sanshray's Portfolio"
  description="A tool for building annotated voice-emotion datasets from scripts and recorded dialogue."
>
  <article class="terminal-page">
    <p class="terminal-prompt">
      C:\PORTFOLIO\PROJECTS&gt; type voice-dataset-builder.txt
    </p>
    <h1>Voice Dataset Builder</h1>

    <p>
      I began this project after my team struggled to find suitable vocal
      datasets for training a custom voice-emotion recognition model for the
      Team HART CUE project.
    </p>

    <p>
      The idea is to match recorded dialogue to scripts using speech-to-text,
      then use the performance directions around each line as emotion labels.
      Television performances can be useful source material because actors
      often communicate emotions clearly and scripts may describe the intended
      delivery.
    </p>

    <div class="resource-block">
      <p>STATUS: IN DEVELOPMENT</p>
      <p>FOCUS: SPEECH TO TEXT // DATA PROCESSING // MACHINE LEARNING</p>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/Sansh-M/VoiceDataSetBuilder"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">[ OPEN GITHUB REPOSITORY ]</a
      >
    </div>

    <nav class="page-actions" aria-label="Page navigation">
      <a href="/">[ RETURN HOME ]</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</ComputerLayout>
